\title{Inner-Product Arguments}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Logarithmic-size proofs without a trusted setup, over ordinary elliptic curve groups. Largely displaced by hash-based schemes in the zkVM setting, so the useful question is where it still wins.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The Bulletproofs-style recursive halving argument and its transcript.}
        \li{Proof size against verifier time: the linear verifier is the catch.}
        \li{Accumulation and the Halo line, as the precursor to modern [folding](dhsorens-003M).}
        \li{Discrete-log security, and the post-quantum consequence.}
    }
}
